messages:
Maya: Quick async standup for Lakeside Analytics (renewal cohort) — hit a surge in onboarding failures in the last 48h. Sharing context and blockers: webhook retries are failing and onboarding emails are delayed. What I did / blockers / today — drop updates below.

Alex: What I did: triaged logs, reproduced the 429 behavior in staging. Looks like our webhook proxy rate-limit bumped unexpectedly (spike from customer). Mitigation: added local retry + exponential backoff. Blocker: need infra approval to increase dedicated queue shard for their org. Today: open PR w/ retry logic, plan to run e2e and smoke tests.

Leon: FYI I pinged infra (infra-channel) and requested a temporary shard bump; they estimated 2-3 hours to schedule change. Also observed some out-of-order messages after retries — possible ordering edge. Adding a short audit job to reconcile and a small fix for idempotency.

Joni: Thanks — Lakeside's CSM escalated this because they have a renewal call tomorrow morning. They asked for ETA and a customer-friendly status note. Also requested logs for the window 03/14 00:00-09:00 PST — ticket #2347 attached.

Alex: quick snippet of the retry handler I pushed to the branch:```js
// simple backoff helper
async function backoff(retries) {
  const delay = Math.min(2000 * Math.pow(2, retries), 30000);
  await sleep(delay);
}
await backoff(retryCount);
```PR will include a small circuit-breaker and counters.

Maya: Blocker: I can't promote the hotfix to prod until infra confirms the shard bump because we risk compounding overload. @Leon can you confirm approval and scheduled time? Also can we offer a temporary app-layer bypass (route to fallback queue) as a stopgap? :pray:

Leon: Confirmed — infra approved the shard bump; scheduling the change at ~22:30 PDT tonight. I'll post the deploy window in infra-channel and attach the runbook. :white_check_mark: I can also flip a quick feature flag to route Lakeside to the fallback queue while we migrate.

support-bot: Ticket #2347 linked to thread — customer: Lakeside Analytics — severity: high — created by Joni.

Alex: I'll cut the hotfix branch now and request review from @Maya and @Joni. Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/compare/hotfix/webhook-retries -> pull/482 (will update once CI passes).

Joni: I'll draft a one-paragraph status update for the renewal call: include ETA for fix (22:30 PDT), mitigation steps (retry + fallback queue), and ask them to hold the call if fix completes before the meeting. Will share copy here for review.

Maya: Today's focus: finish PR, coordinate with Leon for deploy, confirm audit job results, and send the customer note. If anything slips past 21:30 PDT escalate to Carter (head of CS).

Carter: On it — keep me posted. If deploy slips or we need a temporary SLA concession, I'll handle the customer comms during the renewal.

Maya: Great — thanks everyone. I'll post follow-ups as they happen. :thumbsup:
